      <description>&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ac2ef559159d.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ac2d55d4c9e2.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ac2d55d16b2d.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ac2d55d5b8b0.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ac2d55d96d78.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ac2d55d309e3.jpg"/&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Update:&lt;/strong&gt; EUR FIX&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Addition&lt;/em&gt;: Added support for EUR Welcome Amiibo 1.5 and updated the mod files and listing to reflect the changes. USA version remains unchanged&lt;br&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;escape&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NOTICE: This patch utilizes AI-assisted coding. ChatGPT was used to analyze the original game code, troubleshoot errors, and generate the specific replacement code used in this mod.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h2&gt;IMPORTANT UPDATE - EUR Compatibility Fix&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EUR PLAYERS: A corrected version of Permanent Diverse Skin Tones is now available for Welcome Amiibo 1.5.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The previous EUR release targeted the original 1.4 executable and would not function when used with EUR 1.5.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The updated EUR 1.5 release uses corrected executable offsets for both the permanent tanning system and custom skin-tone palettes.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;All six original palettes are included: Default, Warm Honey, Cool Rose, Neutral, Teak, and Soft Fantasy.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;If you are experiencing issues with the previous EUR release, download the updated EUR 1.5 version.&lt;/strong&gt; The original EUR 1.4 release remains available as an archive for players using that version.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;USA PLAYERS: The USA release remains unchanged. No reinstall is necessary.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;Permanent Diverse Skin Tones&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
This is an alternative version of my Inclusive Skin Tone Mod.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
This mod modifies the in-game tanning system to allow for more realistic skin colors while also locking each player's tan level to a permanent value.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
The main reason this version exists is to allow multiple players to have different skin tones within the same game. My Inclusive Skin Tone Mod instead allows players to retain the normal tanning mechanic while using a narrower, more realistic range of skin tones.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
This version is specifically intended for people who:&#13;
&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Do not want the tanning mechanic at all.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Play multiplayer and would still like to have a diverse range of skin tones.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Share a save file with multiple player characters and want each character to have a different skin color.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&#13;
For example, one player with their tan value set to 0 can remain pale-skinned, while another player with their tan value set to 15 can remain dark-skinned.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
Because the tanning mechanic is disabled, these skin tones will not fade over time or become darker from sun exposure.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;Features&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Replaces the normal tanning progression with 8 permanent skin tones.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Allows different player characters to use different skin tones in the same town.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Supports tan values from 0 through 15.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Includes 6 different skin-tone palettes.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Disables automatic tanning and fading.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Supports USA and European Welcome Amiibo releases, including the updated EUR 1.5 revision.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Works with Azahar and Luma3DS / modded 3DS systems.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Uses small IPS patches instead of complete replacement code.bin files.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Allows compatible IPS-based executable modifications to be merged.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Compatible with custom texture packs, with some limitations explained below.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;Important: Region-Specific Downloads&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
This mod supports the USA and European versions of Animal Crossing: New Leaf – Welcome Amiibo.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;strong&gt;The European release has been updated to support Welcome Amiibo version 1.5.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
The USA and EUR versions use different executable code, and different game revisions may also require different patch offsets.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;strong&gt;You MUST download the version that matches your game region and supported revision.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
USA game → Download the USA version.&lt;br&gt;&#13;
European game (Welcome Amiibo 1.5) → Download the updated EUR version.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
Do not use the USA code.ips with a European copy of the game, and do not use the EUR code.ips with a USA copy.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
Using an incompatible patch may cause the mod to not work correctly or prevent the game from booting.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
The updated EUR release includes the same six palettes and features as the USA release.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;Included Palettes&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
The download includes six different color palettes. Each palette is its own version of the mod.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;strong&gt;Only use ONE palette / code.ips at a time.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
Do not combine multiple included palette patches together. Choose the palette you want and install only that version.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
Included palettes:&#13;
&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Default&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Warm Honey&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Cool Rose&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Neutral&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Teak&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Soft Fantasy&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&#13;
If you want the skin colors that most closely resemble the original game, use the included Default version. This retains Nintendo's original skin colors while still disabling the normal tanning mechanic.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;Skin Tone Values&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
Animal Crossing: New Leaf internally stores the tanning level as a value from 0 to 15.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
However, the game displays those values as 8 visible skin-tone levels.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;pre&gt;0-1   = Tone 1&#13;
2-3   = Tone 2&#13;
4-5   = Tone 3&#13;
6-7   = Tone 4&#13;
8-9   = Tone 5&#13;
10-11 = Tone 6&#13;
12-13 = Tone 7&#13;
14-15 = Tone 8&lt;/pre&gt;&#13;
&#13;
For example, values 0 and 1 use the same visible skin tone, while values 14 and 15 use the darkest tone in the selected palette.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
The contact-sheet images on this page use these same value ranges so you can easily see what each tone will look like before changing your character.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;Setting Your Skin Tone&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
Because this mod disables the normal in-game tanning mechanic, your tan value will no longer change naturally.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
Sun exposure will not make your character darker, and your tan will not fade over time.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
You must manually set your desired tan value using either:&#13;
&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;ACNL Save Editor&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Vapecord&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&#13;
Once set, the mod will keep that value permanent.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h3&gt;ACNL Save Editor&lt;/h3&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;ol&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Make a backup of your save before editing it.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Open your garden.dat or garden_plus.dat file in ACNL Save Editor.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Select the player you want to modify.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Find the player's Tan value.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Set it to a value between 0 and 15.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Save your changes.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Restore/import the edited save back into the game.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ol&gt;&#13;
&#13;
You can repeat this for each player character in your town and give each one a different skin tone.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
For example:&#13;
&#13;
&lt;pre&gt;Player 1: 0&#13;
Player 2: 6&#13;
Player 3: 10&#13;
Player 4: 15&lt;/pre&gt;&#13;
&#13;
Each character will keep their selected skin tone permanently.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h3&gt;Vapecord&lt;/h3&gt;&#13;
&#13;
You can also use Vapecord to change your player's tan value directly in-game.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
Use:&#13;
&#13;
&lt;pre&gt;Player Codes &amp;gt; Player Save Codes &amp;gt; Appearance &amp;gt; Tan&lt;/pre&gt;&#13;
&#13;
Set the desired value, then save the game normally.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
After the value has been saved, this mod prevents the normal tanning system from changing it.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;Installation&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;strong&gt;IMPORTANT: This mod uses code.ips instead of code.bin.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
Previous versions of this mod distributed a complete replacement code.bin. If you have an older version installed, remove its code.bin before installing the updated IPS patch.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
Before installing, make sure you downloaded the version matching your game region and supported revision.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
USA copy → USA download.&lt;br&gt;&#13;
European Welcome Amiibo 1.5 copy → Updated EUR download.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h3&gt;Azahar (Emulator)&lt;/h3&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;ol&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Download and extract the appropriate regional release.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Choose the palette/version you want to use.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Right-click Animal Crossing: New Leaf – Welcome Amiibo in Azahar.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Click Open &amp;gt; Mods Location.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Copy your selected palette's code.ips directly into the game's Title ID folder.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Make sure you are only using one version of this mod at a time.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Boot up the game.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ol&gt;&#13;
&#13;
The resulting file structure should look like this:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;strong&gt;USA:&lt;/strong&gt;&#13;
&lt;pre&gt;load/mods/0004000000198E00/code.ips&lt;/pre&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;strong&gt;EUR:&lt;/strong&gt;&#13;
&lt;pre&gt;load/mods/0004000000198F00/code.ips&lt;/pre&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;strong&gt;Do NOT place code.ips inside an exefs folder.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
The IPS file should be directly inside the game's identifier (Title ID) folder.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h3&gt;Luma3DS / Modded 3DS&lt;/h3&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;ol&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Make sure Game Patching is enabled in Luma3DS.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Choose the palette/version you want to use.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Take the code.ips file from that palette's folder.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Place it on your SD card at the path matching your game region.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ol&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;strong&gt;USA:&lt;/strong&gt;&#13;
&lt;pre&gt;luma/titles/0004000000198E00/code.ips&lt;/pre&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;strong&gt;EUR:&lt;/strong&gt;&#13;
&lt;pre&gt;luma/titles/0004000000198F00/code.ips&lt;/pre&gt;&#13;
&#13;
Make sure there is only one code.ips being used for that title.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
Boot up Animal Crossing: New Leaf – Welcome Amiibo.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;Why IPS Instead of code.bin?&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
Previous releases of this mod used complete replacement code.bin files.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
This has now been changed to IPS patches.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
Unlike a full code.bin replacement, an IPS patch contains only the specific executable changes needed for the mod rather than replacing the entire executable.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
This provides several advantages:&#13;
&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Significantly smaller download sizes.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;No need to distribute the entire modified executable.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Easier compatibility with other executable modifications.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to merge compatible IPS patches into a single file.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&#13;
If you are updating from an older release, remove the previous code.bin file before installing the new code.ips.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;IPS Merging / Compatibility With Other Mods&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;strong&gt;Only one code.ips file can be installed in the game's patch location at a time.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
However, unlike complete executable replacements, IPS patches can potentially be merged together.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
If you want to use this mod alongside another IPS-based mod, you can attempt to combine them using &lt;a href="https://ipssafemerger.vercel.app/"&gt;IPS Safe Merger&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
This allows you to combine multiple IPS patches into a single code.ips file.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
For example, you may be able to use this mod alongside another quality-of-life mod that modifies different portions of the game's executable.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;strong&gt;Important compatibility notes:&lt;/strong&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Only merge patches intended for the same game region and version.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Do not merge multiple palettes from this mod together.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Do not place multiple separate code.ips files in the same patch folder.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Some IPS patches may modify the same executable bytes.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Merging does not automatically guarantee compatibility.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;If two patches modify conflicting executable code, they may not work correctly together.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Always keep backups of your original patches before merging.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&#13;
Using IPS files improves the possibility of combining mods, but it does not guarantee that every executable modification will be compatible.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;Compatibility / Limitations&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
This mod currently supports:&#13;
&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Animal Crossing: New Leaf – Welcome Amiibo (USA)&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Animal Crossing: New Leaf – Welcome Amiibo (EUR 1.5)&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&#13;
The European 1.5 release uses updated executable offsets to account for differences between game revisions.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
Make sure you are using the IPS patch intended for your game's region and revision.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
Other regions or unsupported revisions should be considered incompatible unless specifically ported.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
This mod may conflict with other modifications that change the same portions of the game's executable, including:&#13;
&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;ROM hacks that modify executable code.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Other IPS patches that change overlapping code.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Older code.bin replacement mods.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;My Inclusive Skin Tone Mod.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Any other modification that alters the same tanning or skin-color routines.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&#13;
Compatible IPS patches may be merged, but conflicting executable modifications may require additional work to function together.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;Texture Packs&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
This mod will work with custom texture packs.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
However, some textures in New Leaf are designed around the game's original skin colors. If a texture has been manually color-matched to the default skin tones, it may not perfectly match some of the custom palettes in this mod.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
This is especially noticeable with things such as:&#13;
&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Certain clothing textures.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Skin-colored accessories.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Textures containing pre-rendered skin colors.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&#13;
The Default palette should remain the closest match to the original game's artwork.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;Multiplayer / Multiple Player Characters&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
One of the main purposes of this version of the mod is allowing different players to retain different permanent skin tones.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
For example:&#13;
&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Friend A can use Tan 0-1 and remain pale-skinned.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Friend B can use Tan 14-15 and remain dark-skinned.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&#13;
The same applies to multiple player characters living in a single town.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
Each player character can have their own saved tan value, allowing multiple skin tones to coexist in the same save file.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;Additional Color Palettes&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
If there is interest, I can add additional palette options in the future, especially fantasy or stylized palettes.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
If you have a specific palette in mind, feel free to leave it in the comments.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
A palette can consist of any 8 RGB colors.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
For example:&#13;
&#13;
&lt;pre&gt;RGB(255, 220, 200)&#13;
RGB(230, 190, 160)&#13;
RGB(200, 150, 110)&lt;/pre&gt;&#13;
&#13;
The eight colors correspond to the eight visible tan levels shown above.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;Changelog&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;strong&gt;EUR 1.5 Compatibility Update&lt;/strong&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Updated the European IPS patches for Welcome Amiibo version 1.5.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Adjusted executable patch offsets for the European 1.5 revision.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Retained all six existing palettes and permanent tanning functionality.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;No changes to the USA release.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;Important Notes&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Back up your save before using save editors or modifying game files.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Only install one version of this mod at a time.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Do not combine multiple included palette IPS patches.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;The normal tanning mechanic is intentionally disabled.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Changing your skin tone requires ACNL Save Editor or Vapecord.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Make sure you download the version matching your game region and revision.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;USA and EUR versions use different IPS patches.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Remove older code.bin files before installing the new IPS version.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Other IPS mods may be merged only when their executable changes are compatible.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Texture packs are supported, but some pre-colored textures may not perfectly match custom skin palettes.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;Feedback / Requests&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
If you encounter a compatibility issue, visual problem, or have a suggestion for another skin-tone palette, feel free to leave a comment.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
When reporting an issue, please include:&#13;
&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Whether you are using Azahar or a modded 3DS.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Which palette you installed.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Your game region/version.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Whether you are using any other IPS, code.bin, or ROM hack mods.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;If you merged IPS patches, which patches you combined.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&#13;
For additional installation details, please consult the README.txt and QUICK_START.txt included in the download.&lt;/escape&gt;</description>
