      <description>&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ac0685162690.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ad5add2e1b57.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ad5add1b1fc8.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ad5add2d0f4c.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ad5add1b9b4c.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ad5add2bc678.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ad5add1acbe0.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ad5add2b89ed.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ad5add2e1cfc.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ad5add0c694f.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ad5add2d66c2.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ad5add2e5668.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ad5add0cc969.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ad5add0c2f5c.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ad5add0bc8ca.jpg"/&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Update:&lt;/strong&gt; EUR FIX&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Bugfix&lt;/em&gt;: Corrected the EUR 1.5 patch offset, fixing an issue where custom skin tones would not appear in-game.  Please redownload if you are Welcome Amiibo EUR version 1.5&lt;br&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h1&gt;NOTICE: AI-Assisted Development&lt;/h1&gt;&#13;
&#13;
This mod utilizes AI-assisted coding. ChatGPT was used to analyze the original executable code, troubleshoot errors, and generate portions of the replacement code and development tools used in this update.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;IMPORTANT UPDATE - EUR Compatibility Fix&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;strong&gt;EUR PLAYERS: A corrected version is now available for Welcome Amiibo 1.5.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
The previous EUR release targeted the original 1.4 executable and would not appear in updated games&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
The new EUR 1.5 should work in game as intended.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;strong&gt;If you are experiencing issues with the previous EUR release, download the new EUR 1.5 version.&lt;/strong&gt; The original EUR 1.4 release remains available as an archive for players using that version.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;strong&gt;USA PLAYERS: The USA release remains unchanged. No reinstall is necessary.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;Inclusive Skin Tones&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
As many positive things as can be said about the amazing game that is Animal Crossing, it is unfortunate, to say the least, that it took the series nearly 20 years to recognize that skin tones other than white existed.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
In the base game, the only way to change your skin tone is by "tanning" for hours of real-life time to temporarily appear a darker shade.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
Well, no longer.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
With this mod, you can start out with a variety of natural skin tones simply by installing a single patch, while still retaining the game's original tanning mechanic. Your character can gradually deepen their chosen complexion without shifting into an entirely different skin tone.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;strong&gt;Version 2.0 expands the mod to 31 different palettes, providing 248 possible skin-tone appearances across their eight tanning stages!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
Alongside these expanded options, Version 2.0 introduces European region support, new fantasy colors, and smaller IPS patches that can be combined with other compatible executable mods.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;Features&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;248 possible skin-tone appearances&lt;/strong&gt; across 31 selectable palettes, each with eight tanning stages.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;15 natural skin-tone palettes&lt;/strong&gt; covering five complexions: Light, Medium Light, Medium, Medium Dark, and Dark.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3 undertone options&lt;/strong&gt; for every natural complexion: Warm, Cool, and Neutral.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pale Sunburn&lt;/strong&gt;, an alternative tanning progression that gradually becomes redder rather than darker.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;15 fantasy palettes&lt;/strong&gt;, including Rainbow, Pastel, and Grayscale options.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Original tanning mechanic retained.&lt;/strong&gt; Characters can still tan and gradually lose their tan through normal gameplay.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;USA and EUR Welcome Amiibo versions&lt;/strong&gt;, with separate region-specific patches.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;IPS-based installation&lt;/strong&gt; instead of full &lt;code&gt;code.bin&lt;/code&gt; replacements, reducing download size and making compatible executable mods easier to combine.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Compatible with Azahar and Luma3DS/modded 3DS installations.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Compatible with my 4x Upscale Mod and other texture packs.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Individual in-game contact sheets showing all eight tanning stages of each palette.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;strong&gt;Important:&lt;/strong&gt; The 248 appearances are available across all included palettes. Only one palette can be installed at a time, giving your character eight visible tanning stages within that palette.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;Natural Skin Tones&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
There are now &lt;strong&gt;15 natural skin-tone palettes&lt;/strong&gt;, compared with the five included in the original release.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
Each complexion comes in three variations: Warm, Cool, and Neutral.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
The five complexion categories are:&#13;
&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Light&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Medium Light&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Medium&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Medium Dark&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Dark&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&#13;
Rather than shifting into a completely different complexion, each palette has its own eight-stage progression that gradually deepens the selected skin tone.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h3&gt;Pale Sunburn&lt;/h3&gt;&#13;
&#13;
For characters who burn rather than tan, I've also added a separate &lt;strong&gt;Pale Sunburn&lt;/strong&gt; palette.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
Instead of becoming progressively darker, your character's skin gradually becomes redder, beginning with a pale complexion and progressing toward a more pronounced sunburn.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
This uses the existing tanning system rather than introducing a separate sunburn mechanic.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
Combined, the Natural collection includes &lt;strong&gt;16 palettes and 128 possible appearances.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;Fantasy Skin Tones&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
The fantasy collection has also been significantly expanded, increasing from the original three fantasy options to &lt;strong&gt;15 palettes&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h3&gt;Rainbow&lt;/h3&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Red&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Orange&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Yellow&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Green&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Blue&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Indigo&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Violet&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h3&gt;Pastel&lt;/h3&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Pink&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Peach&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Yellow&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Mint&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Blue&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Indigo&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Lavender&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h3&gt;Grayscale&lt;/h3&gt;&#13;
&#13;
An eight-stage grayscale palette progressing from light gray to dark gray.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
Each fantasy palette follows a gradual progression within its own color family. For example, a green character becomes a darker shade of green as their tanning level increases, rather than changing to an entirely different color.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
The Fantasy collection includes &lt;strong&gt;15 palettes and 120 possible appearances.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;Version 2.0 - Major Update&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h3&gt;Regional Support&lt;/h3&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Added region-specific IPS patches for the European version of Animal Crossing: New Leaf - Welcome Amiibo.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Separate USA and EUR downloads are now provided.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;USA and EUR executable patches are not interchangeable.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h3&gt;IPS Conversion&lt;/h3&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Replaced the original full &lt;code&gt;code.bin&lt;/code&gt; distribution with significantly smaller IPS patches.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;IPS files contain only the executable modifications rather than an entire replacement executable.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Compatible executable patches can now be merged without distributing a full replacement &lt;code&gt;code.bin&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h3&gt;Expanded Skin-Tone Selection&lt;/h3&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Increased natural palettes from 5 to 15, including three different undertones.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Added Pale Sunburn as an alternative tanning progression.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Increased fantasy palettes from 3 to 15, including Rainbow, Pastel, and Grayscale options.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Expanded the total selection to 31 palettes and 248 possible appearances.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h3&gt;Improved Previews&lt;/h3&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Added in-game contact sheets showing each palette's eight tanning stages.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Added Natural and Fantasy overview images to make comparing palettes easier.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Each palette's contact sheet is included directly alongside its IPS patch in the download.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h1&gt;Installation&lt;/h1&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;strong&gt;IMPORTANT: Before installing any mods, back up your Animal Crossing: New Leaf save file and any existing executable patches.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
Download the version that matches your game's region and desired collection:&#13;
&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Natural - USA&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Natural - EUR&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Fantasy - USA&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Fantasy - EUR&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&#13;
Each download contains multiple selectable palettes, each with its own &lt;code&gt;code.ips&lt;/code&gt; file and individual contact sheet.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;strong&gt;Only install ONE skin-tone palette at a time.&lt;/strong&gt; Installing multiple palettes simultaneously will not combine their colors and can create conflicts.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;Azahar&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;ol&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Right-click Animal Crossing: New Leaf - Welcome Amiibo in Azahar.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Select &lt;strong&gt;Open &amp;gt; Mods Location&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Open the downloaded ZIP and choose the single skin-tone palette you want to use.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Locate that palette's &lt;code&gt;code.ips&lt;/code&gt; file.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Copy &lt;code&gt;code.ips&lt;/code&gt; directly into the game's Mods Location.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Remove or merge any conflicting existing executable patches before launching the game.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Restart Azahar and launch New Leaf.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ol&gt;&#13;
&#13;
The installed structure should look like this:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;pre&gt;load/mods/TITLE_ID/code.ips&lt;/pre&gt;&#13;
&#13;
Replace &lt;code&gt;TITLE_ID&lt;/code&gt; with the title ID corresponding to your game's region.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;Luma3DS / Modded 3DS&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;ol&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Make sure &lt;strong&gt;Game Patching&lt;/strong&gt; is enabled in Luma3DS.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Choose one skin-tone palette from the correct regional download.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Copy its &lt;code&gt;code.ips&lt;/code&gt; file to the corresponding game's title-ID directory on your SD card.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Remove or merge any conflicting existing executable patches.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Boot Animal Crossing: New Leaf - Welcome Amiibo.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ol&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;strong&gt;USA:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;pre&gt;luma/titles/0004000000198E00/code.ips&lt;/pre&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;strong&gt;EUR:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;pre&gt;luma/titles/0004000000198F00/code.ips&lt;/pre&gt;&#13;
&#13;
Do not use the USA patch with a European game or the EUR patch with a USA game.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;Using This Mod with Other IPS Mods&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
Version 2.0 uses IPS patches rather than complete replacement executables, making it easier to use this mod alongside other compatible code modifications.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
However, &lt;strong&gt;you cannot simply place multiple files named &lt;code&gt;code.ips&lt;/code&gt; in the same location and expect them to work together.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
If you want to use this mod alongside another IPS-based mod, you will need to combine the compatible patches into a single &lt;code&gt;code.ips&lt;/code&gt; file.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h3&gt;IPS Safe Merger&lt;/h3&gt;&#13;
&#13;
You can use the third-party &lt;strong&gt;IPS Safe Merger&lt;/strong&gt; website to help combine compatible IPS patches:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;a href="https://ipssafemerger.vercel.app/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://ipssafemerger.vercel.app/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
This is an external tool and is not developed or maintained by me.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
Before merging:&#13;
&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Back up your save and existing mod files.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Make sure all patches are intended for the same game region and executable version.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Check for overlapping modifications. If two patches modify the same executable bytes differently, they may be incompatible.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Use IPS Safe Merger to combine compatible patches, then install the resulting single &lt;code&gt;code.ips&lt;/code&gt; file.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Test the merged patch carefully before using it for regular gameplay.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;strong&gt;IMPORTANT:&lt;/strong&gt; IPS merging does not guarantee compatibility. Two mods can still conflict even when their executable modifications do not directly overlap, particularly if they change related game functions.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
This skin-tone mod should not be merged with my &lt;strong&gt;Permanent Diverse Skin Tones&lt;/strong&gt; mod, since both modify the same skin-color functionality.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;Compatibility and Important Notes&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Always back up your save before installing, removing, or combining mods.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Keep backups of your existing IPS files and working mod configuration.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Only install one skin-tone palette at a time.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;USA and EUR patches are region-specific and are not interchangeable.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;The game's normal tanning and fading mechanics remain enabled.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Custom texture packs can still be used, including my 4x Upscale Mod.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Some skin-colored artwork, clothing, accessories, and pre-colored textures may not perfectly match certain custom palettes.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Multiplayer compatibility has not been verified. Other players should not be assumed to see your custom skin colors.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Other executable mods may be compatible when properly merged, but compatibility is not guaranteed.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Removing this mod should restore the game's original displayed tanning colors, assuming no other executable modifications affect them.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;For safety, keep a backup of your original mod configuration as well as your save file.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&#13;
If you encounter any bugs, graphical issues, or compatibility problems, please leave a comment with your game region, selected palette, and whether you're using Azahar or a modded 3DS.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;</description>
